id: pm-web-rknk
title: Require edit permission for package catalog mutations in pm-web
description: "The new per-project package catalog routes verified that the caller HAD access to a project but not that the access was WRITABLE. verifyProjectAccess returns a permission field of 'edit' (owner, or an edit share) or 'view' (a view-only share), and the extensions router discarded it.\n\nConsequence: a collaborator holding a view-only share could install, activate, deactivate and uninstall packages on someone else's project. Installing a package changes the workspace for every collaborator, so this is an edit-level action; routes/pm.ts already enforces exactly this for item mutations at line 160 and the new router did not mirror it.\n\nFix: added requireEditableProject(), which resolves the project and rejects a non-edit permission with 403 before any pm command is spawned. Applied to all four mutating routes (install, activate, deactivate, uninstall). The GET listing deliberately stays at read access, so a view-only collaborator can still see which packages a project uses.\n\nAlso removed a redundant resolveNpmSpec(entry.name) lookup guarded by a non-null assertion; the matched catalog entry already carries its own npmSpec constant, so the spawn argument comes straight from the catalog."
type: Issue
status: closed
priority: 2
tags: []
created_at: "2026-07-28T04:06:38.299Z"
updated_at: "2026-07-28T04:06:52.760Z"
closed_at: "2026-07-28T04:06:52.759Z"
author: codex
resolution: fixed
expected_result: "A view-only collaborator receives 403 on every package mutation and no pm command is spawned, while still being able to list the catalog."
actual_result: "All four mutating routes return 403 for a view-only share and the spawn log stays empty; GET returns 200. Negative-controlled: removing the permission check turns the new test red on the first install attempt, so the gate cannot pass vacuously. 156 tests pass, typecheck clean."
close_reason: "Fixed by requiring edit permission on all four mutating catalog routes, with a negative-controlled regression test covering view-only shares."
body: ""
